WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Hello everybody! My name is Markiplier, and welcome back to Subnautica

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.300
Now, I know it's been a long time since I played this,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.500
and ADMITTEDLY, on the last episode that I did,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.700
I didn't even know if I would be playing it again,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.000
because it left on kind of a final note,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.400
getting to the deepest point that was currently in the game.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.700
Now, this is a brand new game that I'm starting,

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.300
and I don't intend to skip forward in it,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.900
because it's been about 5 months

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.900
th-since I last played.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.500
And what is really interesting about the game,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.500
is that it's been updated a lot, as was expected through the procedural

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.500
updating and what-not, ah, every few months.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.400
There is a lot new creatures, a lot new craftables,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.520
and a lot new things like that. But more importantly

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.300
than any of that is, I wanna play this game in terms of

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.600
feeling and exploring the game again.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.600
When I was doing those episodes before,

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.100
it-uh felt like I was showcasing the developer updates,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.300
which is kinda not what the game is about,

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.800
and it's not kinda what I wanted to do for videos.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.100
So, when I was doing the previous videos, and some of

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.100
you guys noticed this, it was like

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.100
the means to the end, the ends to the mean, whatever the phrase is

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.300
I don't even know, I'm not smart enough to know about that.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.400
But it was like, I was doing things

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.800
specifically only to do a specific other thing,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.000
without enjoying what Subnautica was, the ocean that

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.400
you're in. The WONDERFUL environments,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.900
the beautiful, horrific creatures,

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.900
and there are more. The- 
*Inhales*

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.000
The Reaper Leviathan actually is in the game now,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.600
and can shoot FIREBALLS, as far as I know,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.600
but I have intentionally

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.900
NOT looked into the updates.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.800
The many, many updates that there have been,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.500
I have not looked into them, BECAUSE 
I wanna explore it,

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.000
I wanna find it, I wanna see it all,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.000
see everything about it, I wanna know everything about it

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.700
by finding it without having it handed to me.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.100
You know what I mean? I want this to be..
exploration for US,

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.100
and not exploration for the game.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.600
Or whatever it is- I'm trying to say something profound there,

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.000
and it's not entirely working out,
but anyway... LET'S BLAST OFF!

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.360
The only survivor... A lonely solitude incoming!

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.020
And also, they fixed some things about this intro sequence,

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.020
but I don't think they changed very much,

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.820
uh, since the last time I showed it to you guys,

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.820
other than the fact that it's super cool,

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.020
and we still don't know what blew up the ship.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.020
And that is a mystery, like, "What caused this ship

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.020
to blow up?"

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.260
And...

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.620
Was it right it right or wrong in thi- 
Ah, shit, my face-

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:33.140
Was it right or wrong in thinking that, 
there was another ship that came to this planet

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.000
before we did? --Like-- We're obviously..

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.740
either a scientific exploration or-

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.800
or a colonization thing. Like, that's why we're here.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:42.740
But,

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.020
I believe there was some sort of information that

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.180
there was another ship before us.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.860
So anyway, I gotta take care of this bullshit-

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.440
Haaa-booshki!!!! Oh YES...

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.180
Alright, we're good here, everybody good? 
Everybody good?

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.240
Okay, so, now that we're actually in the game,

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.240
I wanna make a few promises to you guys

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.020
that I'm legitimately gonna keep this time.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.040
NUMBER ONE!

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.360
I'm never gonna cheat again.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.140
Not ONCE.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.020
Not NEVER.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.860
Not one time EVER,

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.140
am I gonna cheat again, because 
that ruins the experience of the game.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.220
The other thing about this is:
I.. am alone.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.040
I will have no outside help,

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.400
I'll have no information, other than the 
information you guys give me because

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.820
I'm still gonna be reading you guy's comments in between each episode.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.060
But, in the mean time, I won't be able to put names on lockers-

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.240
-until I'm able to build friggin' lockers.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.900
But they've done a lotta more things--
--A lotta more, A LOTTA more. ;)

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.300
They've done a lot more to improve the 
beginning experience of the game,

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.440
and, by "improve", I mean, "make *Deep voice* HARDER."

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.980
As some of you know, it was a bit easy to get started in the game.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.580
You take 4 titanium, and then do 
your dang ol' thing, and then

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.580
build a base, and then your outta here.
But,

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.740
as far as I know, we're gonna be using this life pod for a good, long time,

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.360
so we better get used to this Bad Boy over there,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.580
and all the wondrous joys that it brings.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.880
So, we're here, and apparently, I can 
get lead out of these things now,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.020
but I'm just gonna be gathering 
resources for a bit to get...started...

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.560
Okay, either I have not payed 
attention to the ocean in a while,

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.540
or... they've added some new sh- Ah.. shit, there we go.

